@startuml 31_seq_device_pairing
title FleetLuma v0.1.0 - Agent initiated pairing (DESIGN ONLY)
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
actor "Device user" as User
participant "Agent Setup UI" as UI
participant "Agent Background Service" as Agent
participant "FastAPI (Vercel)" as API
database "Private PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Flutter Dashboard" as Web
participant "Supabase Auth" as Auth
actor "Authorized operator" as Operator
User -> UI : Connect this device
UI -> Agent : Begin enrollment via local protected IPC
Agent -> Agent : Generate + securely store 256-bit report token
Agent -> API : POST /api/v1/agent/pairings\nreport_token_sha256, device metadata
API -> DB : Create PENDING session; store hashes\n10-minute TTL, rate-limit state
DB --> API : pairing session
API --> Agent : user_code, private device_code, interval=5
Agent --> UI : Show short code + verification URL
Operator -> Web : Sign in and enter displayed code
Web -> Auth : Obtain operator JWT
Auth --> Web : Authenticated JWT
Web -> API : POST /api/v1/operator/pairings/resolve\nBearer operator JWT + code
API -> DB : Check code, TTL, rate limits and membership
DB --> API : Safe device details
API --> Web : Device metadata for confirmation
Operator -> Web : Select workspace and APPROVE
Web -> API : POST /api/v1/operator/pairings/{id}/approve
API -> DB : Atomic authorization, create ACTIVE host\nBind precommitted report-token hash, audit
DB --> API : Authorized host
API --> Web : Approval acknowledged
loop Poll at >=5 seconds, back off if throttled
  Agent -> API : POST /api/v1/agent/pairings/token\nPrivate device_code
  API -> DB : Check private code hash and state
  DB --> API : PENDING / APPROVED / terminal
  API --> Agent : Pending or host_id on approved
end
Agent -> API : POST /api/v1/agent/reports\nBearer locally held reporting token
API -> DB : Check hash + lifecycle ACTIVE\nCommit sample + heartbeat
DB --> API : Accepted
API --> Agent : HTTP 202
Agent --> UI : Connected
Web -> API : GET /api/v1/hosts\nApproved JWT
API --> Web : Real host status and metrics
@enduml
